anically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":[],"title":"urigo/graphql-cli","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:29:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_86ea5abc6f9243168ea093ee895997e9"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_072e51fbae25e526773295d0a2ff9b7074f1170dbbc16e4b5e953a7fe92f7a4b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Plugins are configured through the `extensions` field of the project's GraphQL Config file (`.graphqlrc.yml`), as shown for codegen and diff (`baseSchema`) settings."},{"claim_ids":["clm_28e8e225fdd459e68eb3490e69de9e28102b9bcb45ea232186142099fec1bc18"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented commands include init, codegen (GraphQL Code Generator), generate (Graphback), coverage and diff (GraphQL Inspector), similar and validate (GraphQL Inspector), and serve, which serves a GraphQL server with an in-memory database."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44353a70114b0bb994101b14d91c3b34c5f316e383e786a86cde357ee6d7fb70"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are directed to read the CONTRIBUTING.md guidelines, and the README invites feedback and plugin contributions via the project's Discord channel."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5f15ce7e7b9ef3f951eeecaa96d46cdd6337ac19bba5df7aa3044993f49a4b65"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The `diff` command compares the configured schema against another schema given on the command line as a URL, Git reference, or local file pointer, e.g. `graphql diff git:origin/master:schema.graphql`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_621c23f0fed67734c41c074db6bcb4c673b05de82d83594ffb333eeb39c5ec51"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI is built around GraphQL Config: the config file tells the tools where GraphQL documents and operations live, and the `schema` field accepts URL endpoints, Git URLs, or local file globs and is used by all commands and plugins."},{"claim_ids":["clm_85d2e6c5e459a9c4debfe69bc38d8c3634831d5484052752daa242f1f613ee2b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes an `init` command that asks prompt questions and generates a project with a GraphQL Config setup, and can also generate a project from an existing `.graphqlrc.yml` file's instructions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_979f780a01d6ddc74c5dbb28b6bef53bc0897f685bdd1211cd6bc80c1e430529"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each GraphQL CLI command is a separate npm package installed under the `@graphql-cli/[COMMAND-NAME]` naming scheme, so users can add their own plugins or maintained ones."}],"claim_ids":["clm_072e51fbae25e526773295d0a2ff9b7074f1170dbbc16e4b5e953a7fe92f7a4b","clm_28e8e225fdd459e68eb3490e69de9e28102b9bcb45ea232186142099fec1bc18","clm_44353a70114b0bb994101b14d91c3b34c5f316e383e786a86cde357ee6d7fb70","clm_5f15ce7e7b9ef3f951eeecaa96d46cdd6337ac19bba5df7aa3044993f49a4b65","clm_621c23f0fed67734c41c074db6bcb4c673b05de82d83594ffb333eeb39c5ec51","clm_85d2e6c5e459a9c4debfe69bc38d8c3634831d5484052752daa242f1f613ee2b","clm_979f780a01d6ddc74c5dbb28b6bef53bc0897f685bdd1211cd6bc80c1e430529"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:29:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_86ea5abc6f9243168ea093ee895997e9","id":"pg_3544946196db568c982b3ec18e3354ad","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/urigo-graphql-cli-readme-md-aa709566b74a-3ec18e3354ad.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_78a5f297319957d4a23a3a6411b76b72"],"title":"Urigo/graphql-cli/README.md @ aa709566b74a","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:29:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_86ea5abc6f9243168ea093ee895997e9"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_e290a127ca32f945e7675e72cb8b4ecf24629815ed547f5e623775d81e1398fa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The `codegen` command runs GraphQL Code Generator with no positional arguments, supporting options `--config`/`-c`, `--watch`/`-w`, `--require`/`-r`, `--overwrite`/`-o`, `--silent`/`-s`, and `--project`/`-p`."}],"claim_ids":["clm_e290a127ca32f945e7675e72cb8b4ecf24629815ed547f5e623775d81e1398fa"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:29:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_86ea5abc6f9243168ea093ee895997e9","id":"pg_9aee0f9406aa5dfea9728b2c19b50e5f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/urigo-graphql-cli-website-docs-codegen-md-aa709566b74a-8b2c19b50e5f.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_35979bc0c7115856a164557fc8209d00"],"title":"Urigo/graphql-cli/website/docs/codegen.md @ aa709566b74a","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:29:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_86ea5abc6f9243168ea093ee895997e9"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_32f10a0f778c4da145c4ba86b8cab51e3ca03ec2f760442feda6804396366ab5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Plugin authors use the `defineCommand` utility from `@graphql-cli/common`, returning an object with `command` and `handler` (and optionally a Yargs `builder` for options); errors thrown in a handler report failure back to the CLI host."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cdae27720466d25922ac09f521107c3a966a1a2363c3147211d1a7549e7548fa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI's command management is implemented with Yargs, and plugins/extensions are NodeJS modules written in JavaScript or TypeScript, loaded by name from `node_modules`."}],"claim_ids":["clm_32f10a0f778c4da145c4ba86b8cab51e3ca03ec2f760442feda6804396366ab5","clm_cdae27720466d25922ac09f521107c3a966a1a2363c3147211d1a7549e7548fa"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:29:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_86ea5abc6f9243168ea093ee895997e9","id":"pg_b188494fda245b27a67d47214fecb5c5","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/urigo-graphql-cli-website-docs-custom-commands-md-aa709566b74a-47214fecb5c5.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8b068587ef5b52348e6bfab27deb01b4"],"title":"Urigo/graphql-cli/website/docs/custom-commands.md @ aa709566b74a","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:29:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_86ea5abc6f9243168ea093ee895997e9"}
